@*
    One goal in the Goals view (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#the-goals-view).
    Folded, it is one row: the title, the stacked bar, "5/6 · due 23 Oct" — or "due 23 Oct
    (end of iteration)" for a goal without a due date of its own — and its forecast badge,
    and a chevron at its end that points down folded and up open. A press
    anywhere on that row opens the goal, or folds the open one; the title is its button,
    which the keyboard reaches and which carries aria-expanded. Nothing in the body
    toggles. Opened, the bar runs under the title and the goal lists what is
    attached to it in three columns — Plan with each plan's done/total, Tasks with a
    status dot each, Pull requests with a status line each, the merged ones gathered
    on one line as pills and "merged" — and below them the attach search.

    The search matches the host's candidates — plans, tasks and pull requests — by
    title, or a pull request by its number, and lists each match under its kind label.
    A query is tried as typed and with one leading + or # dropped, since a plan is titled
    with its bare slug and the app writes its tag as +slug; a title that holds the sigil
    still matches as typed.
    A query that names a pull request — #N or N, read in each of the host's Repositories,
    owner/name#N, or its GitHub address — leads the list with it, titled with its
    repository, even when no candidate holds it: attaching names it by identity alone.
    Picking one hands its GoalSubject back through OnAttach and puts the focus back in the
    search box; the host attaches it — through the GoalPicker, which
    names the other goal and asks first, when another goal holds it — and reads the view
    again. It is a list of matches over the view's own candidates; choosing the goal is
    GoalPicker's.

    With a host listening on OnQuickAdd, a query that is not blank ends the list with
    "New task “‹query›”", shown even when nothing matches. Picking it hands the trimmed
    query back; the host creates the task and attaches it. Once a task exists that did not
    before — on the goal, or among the candidates when the attach after the create was
    refused — the query clears and the focus goes back to the search box, as a pick does, so
    the row cannot create the task twice; a refused create leaves the typed text. The row
    waits while the host writes.

    With a host listening on OnEdit, the open goal leads with its title, outcome and due
    date as fields, edited in place (.devbook/design/interaction-guidelines.md
    #auto-save-no-save-buttons): there is no Save button, a field is handed back when it
    changes — on leaving it, on Enter, on a picked date — with the other two as stored,
    and a value the goal already says is not handed back. Escape abandons what was typed
    in a field and stops there (interaction-guidelines.md#task-rows). A value handed back
    stays the field's until a reading says otherwise, so a second edit sent before the
    first one's reading lands carries both. The module owns the rules, so a blank title or
    a second outcome line comes back as the module's refusal in EditError, on the refused
    field, and the field shows what the goal still says — written back onto the same
    input, so the focus stays (the way ImpedimentRow's picker does it). The Due field holds
    the goal's own date, empty for a goal without one: the iteration end such a goal is
    shown due on is read, never handed back as its date. Emptying the field clears the
    date; a date the field cannot read is not handed back, and leaving the field puts the
    goal's date back. The date is handed back on leaving the field or Enter, never per
    keystroke, since a date field reads 0002, 0020 and 0202 on its way to a typed year.
    Delete goal… sits beside them and asks first, through the board's ConfirmDialog.
    Without a listener the outcome is a line of text and nothing is editable.

    With a host listening on OnDetach, each Plan, Tasks and Pull requests row the goal
    holds itself carries an icon-only Detach, named for the item. A pull request the goal
    holds only through one of its tasks has none: detaching the task is what lets it go.
    Detaching changes nothing on the item, so it does not ask; the focus then waits in the
    attach search, since the row goes with the next reading.

    With a host listening on OnMove, the head row leads with a grip and carries Move up and
    Move down before the chevron, each named for the goal; a press on any of them neither
    opens nor folds the goal. The grip is a press origin for the library's shared pointer
    reorder (data-reorder-grip on a data-reorder-item); the board owns the drag. Move up
    and Move down hand -1 or +1 back, are disabled at the ends (CanMoveUp, CanMoveDown) and
    while the host writes, and keep the focus on the button pressed — on the other one once
    the goal has reached that end. Dragging draws the goal held set back, in the place it
    would land.

    The forecast badge is the forecast family of .devbook/design/color-scheme.md
    #goal-forecast-badges: At risk takes the fault fill with its own ink as edge, On
    track the settled fill inside the strong edge.
*@
@inject IJSRuntime Js
<section class="@ClassValue"
         aria-labelledby="@TitleId"
         data-testid="@TestId"
         data-expanded="@(Expanded ? "true" : "false")"
         data-reorder-item="@(CanMove ? Goal.Id : null)"
         data-draggable="@(CanMove ? "true" : null)">
    @* The whole head row opens and folds the goal: most of a folded row is its bar, its
       line and the space between them, not its title. The title stays the one control
       the keyboard reaches and the one that says expanded; its press stops at itself so
       the row does not toggle a second time. *@
    <div class="goal-card__head" @onclick="() => OnToggle.InvokeAsync()" data-testid="@Part("head")">
        @if (CanMove)
        {
            @* The grip is a press origin for the shared pointer reorder and nothing else, so
               a press on it never opens or folds the goal; the keyboard moves the goal with
               Move up and Move down. *@
            <span class="goal-card__grip" data-reorder-grip aria-hidden="true" @onclick:stopPropagation="true" data-testid="@Part("grip")">⠿</span>
        }
        <h3 class="goal-card__title" id="@TitleId">
            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                       BaseClass="goal-card__toggle"
                       OnClick="() => OnToggle.InvokeAsync()"
                       StopPropagation="true"
                       aria-expanded="@(Expanded ? "true" : "false")"
                       aria-controls="@(Expanded ? BodyId : null)"
                       TestId="@Part("toggle")">@Goal.Title</AppButton>
        </h3>
        @if (!Expanded)
        {
            <GoalProgressBar Counts="Goal.Counts" CssClass="goal-card__bar" TestId="@Part("bar")" />
        }
        <span class="goal-card__meta" data-testid="@Part("meta")">@GoalsText.GoalLine(Goal)</span>
        <Badge Kind="forecast" Slug="@(Goal.AtRisk ? "at-risk" : "on-track")" TestId="@Part("forecast")">@GoalsText.Forecast(Goal.AtRisk)</Badge>
        @if (CanMove)
        {
            <span class="goal-card__moves" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                <IconButton AriaLabel="@($"Move {Goal.Title} up")"
                            Title="Move up"
                            Disabled="@(Busy || !CanMoveUp)"
                            CssClass="goal-card__move"
                            OnClick="() => MoveAsync(-1)"
                            id="@MoveId(-1)"
                            TestId="@Part("move-up")">
                    <ChevronUpIcon Size="14" />
                </IconButton>
                <IconButton AriaLabel="@($"Move {Goal.Title} down")"
                            Title="Move down"
                            Disabled="@(Busy || !CanMoveDown)"
                            CssClass="goal-card__move goal-card__move--down"
                            OnClick="() => MoveAsync(1)"
                            id="@MoveId(1)"
                            TestId="@Part("move-down")">
                    <ChevronUpIcon Size="14" />
                </IconButton>
            </span>
        }
        <span class="@(Expanded ? "goal-card__chevron goal-card__chevron--open" : "goal-card__chevron")" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="@Part("chevron")">
            <ChevronUpIcon />
        </span>
    </div>

    @if (Expanded)
    {
        <GoalProgressBar Counts="Goal.Counts" Large="true" TestId="@Part("bar")" />

        <div class="goal-card__body" id="@BodyId">
            @if (CanEdit)
            {
                <div class="goal-card__details" data-testid="@Part("details")">
                    <div class="goal-card__fields">
                        @FieldBox(GoalField.Title, "Title", "text", null)
                        @FieldBox(GoalField.Outcome, "Outcome", "text", "One line on what is true once it lands")
                        @FieldBox(GoalField.Due, "Due date", "date", null)
                    </div>
                    @if (OnDelete.HasDelegate)
                    {
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Danger"
                                   Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                   Disabled="Busy"
                                   CssClass="goal-card__delete"
                                   OnClick="() => OnDelete.InvokeAsync()"
                                   TestId="@Part("delete")">Delete goal…</AppButton>
                    }
                </div>
                <Alert Message="@(_refused is null ? EditError : null)" TestId="@Part("edit-error")" />
            }
            else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Goal.Outcome))
            {
                <p class="goal-card__outcome" data-testid="@Part("outcome")">@Goal.Outcome</p>
            }

            <div class="goal-card__columns">
                <div class="goal-card__column" data-testid="@Part("plans")">
                    <span class="goal-card__column-title">Plan</span>
                    @foreach (var plan in Goal.Plans)
                    {
                        <span class="goal-card__plan">
                            <span class="goal-card__plan-title">@plan.Title</span>
                            <span class="goal-card__plan-count">@plan.Done/@plan.Total</span>
                            @Detach(plan.Subject, $"plan {plan.Title}")
                        </span>
                    }
                    @if (Goal.Plans.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <span class="goal-card__none">None</span>
                    }
                </div>

                <div class="goal-card__column" data-testid="@Part("tasks")">
                    <span class="goal-card__column-title">Tasks</span>
                    @foreach (var task in Goal.Tasks)
                    {
                        <span class="goal-card__task" data-status="@task.Status.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()">
                            <StatusDot Tone="@Tone(task.Status)" />
                            <span class="goal-card__task-title">@task.Title</span>
                            <span class="sr-only">, @StatusWords(task.Status)</span>
                            @Detach(task.Subject, $"task {task.Title}")
                        </span>
                    }
                    @if (Goal.Tasks.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <span class="goal-card__none">None</span>
                    }
                </div>

                <div class="goal-card__column" data-testid="@Part("pull-requests")">
                    <span class="goal-card__column-title">Pull requests</span>
                    @foreach (var (pull, subject) in Pulls.Where(p => !p.Pull.IsMerged))
                    {
                        <span class="goal-card__pull">
                            <PullRequestStatus Model="pull" TestId="@Part($"pull-request-{pull.Number}")" />
                            @Detach(subject, $"pull request #{pull.Number}")
                        </span>
                    }
                    @if (Merged.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <span class="goal-card__merged" data-testid="@Part("merged")">
                            @foreach (var (pull, subject) in Merged)
                            {
                                <span class="goal-card__merged-pull">
                                    <Badge Kind="gh" Slug="merged" Href="@pull.Url" Title="@pull.Title">#@pull.Number</Badge>
                                    @Detach(subject, $"pull request #{pull.Number}")
                                </span>
                            }
                            <span>merged</span>
                        </span>
                    }
                    @if (Goal.PullRequests.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <span class="goal-card__none">None</span>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="goal-card__attach">
                <SearchBox @ref="_search"
                           Value="@_query"
                           ValueChanged="value => _query = value"
                           Placeholder="@AttachLabel"
                           AriaLabel="@AttachLabel"
                           DebounceMilliseconds="0"
                           CssClass="goal-card__search"
                           TestId="@Part("attach")" />
                @if (Matches.Count > 0 || QuickAddTitle is not null)
                {
                    <ul class="goal-card__matches" aria-label="Matches" data-testid="@Part("matches")">
                        @foreach (var match in Matches)
                        {
                            <li class="goal-card__match-row">
                                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                           BaseClass="goal-card__match"
                                           OnClick="() => PickAsync(match)"
                                           TestId="@Part($"match-{match.Subject.Key}")">
                                    <span class="goal-card__match-kind">@KindLabel(match.Kind)</span>
                                    <span class="goal-card__match-title">
                                        @if (match.Number is { } number)
                                        {
                                            <span class="goal-card__number">#@number</span>@(" ")
                                        }
                                        @match.Title
                                    </span>
                                </AppButton>
                            </li>
                        }
                        @if (QuickAddTitle is { } title)
                        {
                            <li class="goal-card__match-row">
                                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                           BaseClass="goal-card__match"
                                           CssClass="goal-card__match--new"
                                           Disabled="Busy"
                                           OnClick="() => QuickAddAsync(title)"
                                           TestId="@Part("quick-add")">
                                    <span class="goal-card__match-kind">New</span>
                                    <span class="goal-card__match-title">New task “@title”</span>
                                </AppButton>
                            </li>
                        }
                    </ul>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>The most matches the attach search lists at once.</summary>
    public const int MatchLimit = 8;

    /// <summary>The attach search's placeholder and accessible name.</summary>
    public const string AttachLabel = "Attach a plan, task or pull request";

    private readonly string _id = "goal-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
    private string _query = string.Empty;
    private SearchBox? _search;
    private bool _focusSearch;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public GoalCardModel Goal { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Whether the goal is open, with its columns and the attach search.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Expanded { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The title, or anywhere on the head row, was pressed: open the goal, or fold
    /// it.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnToggle { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A field of the open goal changed: its title, outcome and due date, the other
    /// two as stored. Without a listener nothing on the goal is editable.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalEditRequest> OnEdit { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Delete goal… was pressed; the board asks first. Without a listener there is
    /// no Delete goal….</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnDelete { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A row's Detach was pressed: the item it is for. Without a listener no row has
    /// one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalSubject> OnDetach { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Why the last edit was refused, in the module's words, under the fields.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? EditError { get; set; }

    /// <summary>While the host writes: Delete goal… and Detach wait. The fields stay live so
    /// the focus is never taken from under the person.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Busy { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the attach search matches over.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> Candidates { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The repositories a bare pull request number in the attach search is read
    /// in, <c>owner/name</c> each, so a pull request no candidate holds can be attached by
    /// its number. Empty reads a bare number against <see cref="Candidates"/> alone.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Repositories { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>A match was picked: the work it names.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalSubject> OnAttach { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The "New task" row was picked: the title typed, trimmed, for the host to
    /// create a task with and attach. Without a listener there is no such row.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnQuickAdd { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Move up or Move down was pressed: -1 or +1, one place. Without a listener the
    /// goal has no grip and no Move buttons and cannot be picked up.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<int> OnMove { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether a goal sits above this one, so Move up has somewhere to go.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool CanMoveUp { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether a goal sits below this one, so Move down has somewhere to go.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool CanMoveDown { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the goal is the one held in a drag, which the board draws in the
    /// place it would land.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Dragging { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Lands on the section; its parts take it as a prefix.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    private string TitleId => _id + "-title";

    private string BodyId => _id + "-body";

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var expanded = Expanded ? " goal-card--expanded" : string.Empty;
            var dragging = Dragging ? " goal-card--dragging" : string.Empty;
            var extra = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? string.Empty : " " + CssClass;
            return $"goal-card{expanded}{dragging}{extra}";
        }
    }

    private bool CanEdit => OnEdit.HasDelegate;

    private bool CanMove => OnMove.HasDelegate;

    private string MoveId(int direction) => _id + (direction < 0 ? "-move-up" : "-move-down");

    /// <summary>The Move button to give the focus back to once the goal has moved, or null.</summary>
    private int? _focusMove;

    /// <summary>Hands the move to the board. The goal's element is moved, not drawn again,
    /// so the focus is put back on the Move button pressed — or on the other one, once the
    /// goal has reached the end the pressed one pointed at.</summary>
    private async Task MoveAsync(int direction)
    {
        await OnMove.InvokeAsync(direction);
        _focusMove = direction;
    }

    /// <summary>Each pull request with its subject, in the goal's order.</summary>
    private List<(PullRequestStatusModel Pull, GoalSubject? Subject)> Pulls =>
        [.. Goal.PullRequests.Select((pull, index) => (pull, Goal.PullRequestSubject(index)))];

    private List<(PullRequestStatusModel Pull, GoalSubject? Subject)> Merged => [.. Pulls.Where(p => p.Pull.IsMerged)];

    /// <summary>A row's Detach, named for <paramref name="what"/>; nothing without a subject
    /// or a listener.</summary>
    private RenderFragment Detach(GoalSubject? subject, string what) => __builder =>
    {
        if (subject is null || !OnDetach.HasDelegate) return;

        <IconButton AriaLabel="@($"Detach {what} from {Goal.Title}")"
                    Title="@($"Detach from {Goal.Title}")"
                    Disabled="Busy"
                    CssClass="goal-card__detach"
                    OnClick="() => DetachAsync(subject)"
                    TestId="@Part($"detach-{subject.Key}")">
            <XIcon Size="14" />
        </IconButton>
    };

    /// <summary>The due date as a date field writes it.</summary>
    public static string DueText(DateOnly day) => day.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);

    private enum GoalField { Title, Outcome, Due }

    // Per field, as text: what the person has typed since the field last drew a value; what
    // was handed back and the goal does not say yet, so a second edit sent before the first
    // one's reading lands carries it rather than the stored value; and a value drawn for one
    // render only, so the stored one is then written back onto the same input and the focus
    // stays where it is.
    private readonly Dictionary<GoalField, string> _typed = [];
    private readonly Dictionary<GoalField, string> _pending = [];
    private readonly Dictionary<GoalField, string> _override = [];
    private readonly Dictionary<GoalField, string> _seen = [];
    private string? _seenGoalId;
    private GoalField? _refused;

    private RenderFragment FieldBox(GoalField field, string label, string type, string? placeholder) => __builder =>
    {
        <div class="goal-card__field-box"
             @onkeydown="key => FieldKeyAsync(field, key)"
             @onkeydown:stopPropagation="@_typed.ContainsKey(field)"
             @onfocusout="() => LeaveAsync(field)">
            <TextField Label="@label"
                       Type="@type"
                       Value="@Shown(field)"
                       ValueChanged="value => _typed[field] = value"
                       Placeholder="@placeholder"
                       Compact="true"
                       ErrorMessage="@(_refused == field ? EditError : null)"
                       CssClass="@($"goal-card__field goal-card__field--{Slug(field)}")"
                       TestId="@Part(Slug(field))"
                       @onchange="change => ChangedAsync(field, change.Value as string)" />
        </div>
    };

    private static string Slug(GoalField field) => field switch
    {
        GoalField.Title => "title",
        GoalField.Outcome => "outcome",
        _ => "due"
    };

    private string Stored(GoalField field) => field switch
    {
        GoalField.Title => Goal.Title,
        GoalField.Outcome => Goal.Outcome ?? string.Empty,
        // The goal's own date: a derived iteration end is shown, never handed back as one.
        _ => Goal.OwnDueDate is { } own ? DueText(own) : string.Empty
    };

    /// <summary>What the field holds: the value handed back while the goal does not say it
    /// yet, the stored one otherwise.</summary>
    private string Current(GoalField field) => _pending.TryGetValue(field, out var pending) ? pending : Stored(field);

    private string Shown(GoalField field) => _override.TryGetValue(field, out var drawn) ? drawn : Current(field);

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (_seenGoalId != Goal.Id)
        {
            _seenGoalId = Goal.Id;
            _typed.Clear();
            _pending.Clear();
            _seen.Clear();
            _refused = null;
        }

        // A reading that changes a field - this edit landing, or anyone's - is the newest
        // word on it: the value handed back gives way.
        foreach (var field in Enum.GetValues<GoalField>())
        {
            var stored = Stored(field);
            if (_seen.TryGetValue(field, out var seen) && seen != stored) _pending.Remove(field);
            _seen[field] = stored;
            if (_pending.TryGetValue(field, out var pending) && pending == stored) _pending.Remove(field);
        }

        if (EditError is null) _refused = null;
    }

    private static string? Clean(string? text) => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(text) ? null : text.Trim();

    /// <summary>Whether the Due field's text is one to hand back: a date, or empty, which
    /// clears the goal's date.</summary>
    private static bool SettlesDue(string text) => text.Length == 0 || ReadDue(text) is not null;

    private static DateOnly? ReadDue(string? text) =>
        DateOnly.TryParseExact(text?.Trim(), "yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,
            System.Globalization.DateTimeStyles.None, out var day) ? day : null;

    /// <summary>Hands the three back once a field changes, each the value the card holds
    /// for it. A value the field already holds is not handed back, and neither is a date
    /// the field cannot read - leaving it puts the goal's date back. A refusal, read once
    /// the host has answered, puts the stored value back on the same input and names the
    /// field.</summary>
    private async Task CommitAsync(GoalField field, string? raw)
    {
        _typed.Remove(field);
        var value = field switch
        {
            GoalField.Due => (raw ?? string.Empty).Trim(),
            _ => Clean(raw) ?? string.Empty
        };

        if (field == GoalField.Due && !SettlesDue(value))
        {
            // Kept as typed, so leaving the field puts the goal's date back.
            _typed[field] = value;
            return;
        }

        if (value == Current(field)) return;

        _pending[field] = value;
        _refused = null;
        await OnEdit.InvokeAsync(new GoalEditRequest(
            Goal.Id,
            Current(GoalField.Title),
            Clean(Current(GoalField.Outcome)),
            ReadDue(Current(GoalField.Due))));

        // Let the host's answer render, so EditError is this edit's.
        await Task.Yield();
        if (EditError is null || !_pending.TryGetValue(field, out var sent) || sent != value) return;

        _pending.Remove(field);
        _refused = field;
        await DrawAgainAsync(field, value);
    }

    /// <summary>Escape abandons what was typed in the field and stops there.</summary>
    private async Task FieldKeyAsync(GoalField field, KeyboardEventArgs key)
    {
        if (key.Key == "Enter" && field == GoalField.Due)
        {
            await SettleDueAsync();
            return;
        }

        if (key.Key != "Escape" || !_typed.Remove(field, out var typed)) return;

        await DrawAgainAsync(field, typed);
    }

    /// <summary>A text field is handed back on its change — leaving it or Enter. A date
    /// field changes on every keystroke that makes a whole date, so typing a year passes
    /// through 0002, 0020 and 0202: it is only held, and handed back on leaving or Enter.</summary>
    private Task ChangedAsync(GoalField field, string? raw)
    {
        if (field != GoalField.Due) return CommitAsync(field, raw);

        _typed[field] = (raw ?? string.Empty).Trim();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private Task LeaveAsync(GoalField field) => field == GoalField.Due ? SettleDueAsync() : Task.CompletedTask;

    /// <summary>Hands the held date back — an empty field as no date — or puts the goal's
    /// date back when the field cannot read what it holds.</summary>
    private async Task SettleDueAsync()
    {
        if (!_typed.TryGetValue(GoalField.Due, out var typed)) return;

        if (SettlesDue(typed))
        {
            await CommitAsync(GoalField.Due, typed);
            return;
        }

        _typed.Remove(GoalField.Due);
        await DrawAgainAsync(GoalField.Due, typed);
    }

    /// <summary>Draws <paramref name="was"/> for one render and then the value the card
    /// holds, so the field writes it back onto the same input rather than a new one.</summary>
    private async Task DrawAgainAsync(GoalField field, string was)
    {
        _override[field] = was;
        StateHasChanged();
        await Task.Yield();
        _override.Remove(field);
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    private async Task DetachAsync(GoalSubject subject)
    {
        await OnDetach.InvokeAsync(subject);
        await Task.Yield();

        // The row goes with the reading: the focus waits in the attach search. A refused
        // detach leaves the row, and the focus on its Detach.
        _focusSearch = !Holds(subject);
    }

    private bool Holds(GoalSubject subject) =>
        Goal.Plans.Any(plan => plan.Subject == subject)
        || Goal.Tasks.Any(task => task.Subject == subject)
        || Enumerable.Range(0, Goal.PullRequests.Count).Any(index => Goal.PullRequestSubject(index) == subject);

    private IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> Matches => Match(Candidates, _query, Repositories);

    /// <summary>The title the "New task" row offers: the query trimmed, while a host listens
    /// and the query is not blank.</summary>
    private string? QuickAddTitle =>
        OnQuickAdd.HasDelegate && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_query) ? _query.Trim() : null;

    private string? Part(string part) => TestId is null ? null : $"{TestId}-{part}";

    /// <summary>The candidates <see cref="IsMatch"/> keeps for <paramref name="query"/>; none
    /// for a blank query.</summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> Match(IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> candidates, string? query) =>
        [.. Matching(candidates, query).Take(MatchLimit)];

    private static IEnumerable<GoalsItem> Matching(IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> candidates, string? query) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(query) ? [] : candidates.Where(item => IsMatch(item, query));

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether <paramref name="item"/> answers <paramref name="query"/>, ignoring case: its
    /// title holds the query as typed or with one leading <c>+</c> or <c>#</c> dropped — a
    /// plan is titled with its bare slug, and the app writes its tag as <c>+slug</c> — or
    /// its number starts with the query, a leading <c>#</c> ignored. A blank query answers
    /// every item.
    /// </summary>
    public static bool IsMatch(GoalsItem item, string? query)
    {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(item);

        var text = query?.Trim() ?? string.Empty;
        if (text.Length == 0) return true;

        var bare = text[0] is '+' or '#' ? text[1..].TrimStart() : string.Empty;
        var number = text.TrimStart('#');
        return item.Title.Contains(text, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
               || (bare.Length > 0 && item.Title.Contains(bare, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
               || (number.Length > 0 && item.Number is { } n
                   && n.ToString(System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture).StartsWith(number, StringComparison.Ordinal));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// <see cref="Match(IReadOnlyList{GoalsItem}, string?)"/>, led by the pull requests
    /// <paramref name="query"/> names (<see cref="PullRequestReference.Resolve"/>) — a bare
    /// number in each of <paramref name="repositories"/> — so one no candidate holds can be
    /// attached by identity, titled with its repository. A pull request a candidate holds is
    /// listed once, as that candidate. Every named pull request is listed; <see cref="MatchLimit"/>
    /// caps only the candidate matches after them, so no registered repository goes unoffered.
    /// </summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> Match(IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> candidates, string? query, IReadOnlyList<string> repositories)
    {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(candidates);

        List<GoalsItem> named = [.. PullRequestReference.Resolve(query, repositories)
            .Select(subject => candidates.FirstOrDefault(item => SamePullRequest(item.Subject, subject))
                               ?? new GoalsItem(subject, subject.Repository!))
            .DistinctBy(Key)];

        var listed = named.Select(Key).ToHashSet(StringComparer.Ordinal);

        return [.. named.Concat(Matching(candidates, query)
            .Where(item => !listed.Contains(Key(item)))
            .DistinctBy(Key)
            .Take(MatchLimit))];
    }

    private static string Key(GoalsItem item) => item.Subject.Key.ToUpperInvariant();

    private static bool SamePullRequest(GoalSubject left, GoalSubject right) =>
        left.Kind == GoalSubjectKind.PullRequest
        && right.Kind == GoalSubjectKind.PullRequest
        && left.Number == right.Number
        && string.Equals(left.Repository, right.Repository, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>The kind label a match or a No goal row reads under.</summary>
    public static string KindLabel(GoalSubjectKind kind) => kind switch
    {
        GoalSubjectKind.Plan => "Plan",
        GoalSubjectKind.Task => "Task",
        _ => "PR"
    };

    private async Task PickAsync(GoalsItem match)
    {
        // The pick clears the query, which takes the list and the focused button with it:
        // the focus goes back to the search box once the list is gone.
        _query = string.Empty;
        _focusSearch = true;
        await OnAttach.InvokeAsync(match.Subject);
    }

    /// <summary>Hands the title back for the host to create and attach. Once a task exists
    /// that did not before — held by the goal, or among the candidates when the attach after
    /// the create was refused — the query clears and the focus goes back to the search box,
    /// as a pick does, so the row cannot create it a second time. A refused create leaves the
    /// typed text, to change and try again.</summary>
    private async Task QuickAddAsync(string title)
    {
        var known = TasksKnown();

        await OnQuickAdd.InvokeAsync(title);
        await Task.Yield();

        if (TasksKnown().IsSubsetOf(known)) return;

        _query = string.Empty;
        _focusSearch = true;
    }

    /// <summary>Every task the card can see: the goal's own and the candidates'.</summary>
    private HashSet<string> TasksKnown() =>
    [
        .. Goal.Tasks.Select(task => "goal:" + task.Id),
        .. Candidates.Where(item => item.Kind == GoalSubjectKind.Task).Select(item => item.Subject.Key)
    ];

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (_focusMove is { } direction)
        {
            _focusMove = null;
            var stillGoes = direction < 0 ? CanMoveUp : CanMoveDown;
            await global::Backlog.UI.Components.Tasks.QuickEditField.FocusAsync(Js, MoveId(stillGoes ? direction : -direction), select: false);
        }

        if (!_focusSearch || _search is null) return;

        _focusSearch = false;
        await _search.FocusAsync();
    }

    private static FlowStepTone Tone(GoalTaskStatus status) => status switch
    {
        GoalTaskStatus.Done => FlowStepTone.Done,
        GoalTaskStatus.Doing => FlowStepTone.Active,
        GoalTaskStatus.Blocked => FlowStepTone.Blocked,
        _ => FlowStepTone.Pending
    };

    private static string StatusWords(GoalTaskStatus status) => status switch
    {
        GoalTaskStatus.Done => "done",
        GoalTaskStatus.Doing => "in progress",
        GoalTaskStatus.Blocked => "blocked",
        _ => "not started"
    };
}
